message.content:
{
  "summary": "This bill proposes changes to how public charter schools are authorized and renewed. It would allow a public charter school authorized by the commission and the local board of education of the local education agency (LEA) where the school is located to mutually agree in writing, within 30 calendar days of authorization, that the local board of education will serve as both the authorizer and the LEA. In this case, the local board would take over the rights and responsibilities of the charter agreement, which must be filed with the commission. This option is not available to schools that had their charter agreement renewed on appeal by the commission. Additionally, the bill would specify that if a local board of education approves a charter school renewal application, the renewed agreement must last for 10 academic years. If the commission approves the renewal, the term must be between five and ten academic years, as decided by the commission. The bill also changes certain technical references to \"initial charter agreements\" and removes specific \"notwithstanding\" clauses in the law. These changes would take effect immediately upon becoming law."
}
